.TH STRALLOC_ALLOC 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
stralloc_alloc \- Allocate memory for a stralloc

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/stralloc.h>

.IB void
.IB stralloc_alloc(stralloc* sa);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBstralloc_alloc\fR function allocates memory for the stralloc \fIsa\fR based on its current length and sets the allocated size.

.SH PARAMETERS
.IB sa
The stralloc for which memory will be allocated.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The \fBstralloc_alloc\fR function does not return a value.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBstralloc_alloc\fR function to allocate memory for a stralloc:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/stralloc.h>

int main() {
    stralloc sa;
    stralloc_init(&sa);

    // Your code to use the stralloc here

    stralloc_alloc(&sa);

    // Your code to use the allocated memory here

    stralloc_done(&sa);

    return 0;
}
.nef